  "correctAnswer": "C",
  "explanation": "Choice C is correct. A number that is $67$ more than $x$ can be represented by the expression $x + 67$. The function $g$ gives the product of $x$ and this quantity, so $g(x) = x(x + 67)$. Distributing yields $g(x) = x^{2} + 67x$.\n\nWhy A is incorrect:\n\nChoice A is incorrect. This expression results from adding $67$ as a constant rather than distributing $x$ through $(x + 67)$; the correct product $x \\cdot 67$ is $67x$, not $67$.",
